{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L14-CHECKIN","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.4","block_identifier":"scenario-call-time","question_identifier":"q14a","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"For the recurring call structures evidenced here, call time means being ready and available through the controlling check-in/reporting process rather than merely reaching the property at that clock time; exact arrival/check-in rules remain call-specific.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"work_readiness","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Do not invent one nationally required number of minutes early."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L14-REPORTBACK","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1/5","lesson_identifier":"1.4/5.2","block_identifier":"task-complete-availability","question_identifier":"q14b/q62","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"When assigned work is actually complete, report completion or return through the established lead/steward/department process and remain available as directed; do not self-assign into another department or assume task completion creates a break or release.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact reassignment, standby and break process varies by employer/local/CBA/production."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L14-LIMITS","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1/9","lesson_identifier":"1.4/9.1–9.3","block_identifier":"specialized-work-limit","question_identifier":"q14c","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"If an unfamiliar or specialized task exceeds the learner's training, assignment or authority, the learner should state the limitation and seek instruction or another assignment rather than bluffing or treating one observation as authorization.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Course completion/observation does not create employer authorization or specialist qualification."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L43-CABLE-OWNERSHIP","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-FLD","D-LTG","D-AUD","D-VID","D-ELC"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.3","block_identifier":"new-space-hazards","question_identifier":"q43","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"An unfamiliar production cable that appears idle is not automatically released to move; identify the owning department/person and get the appropriate direction before changing it.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Transferable work-control boundary requiring department/practitioner validation; it does not authorize technical cable actions."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L43-PIT-PEDESTRIAN","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-LOG"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.3","block_identifier":"new-space-hazards","question_identifier":"q43","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Powered-industrial-truck environments can include pedestrian traffic, blind/restricted areas and ramps; a general stagehand remains clear of the operating environment and does not operate covered equipment without the employer's required training/evaluation.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Limited to powered industrial trucks within OSHA scope; other powered equipment has its own requirements."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L43-ROUTE-VERIFY","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-OUT","D-ACC"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.3","block_identifier":"new-space-hazards","question_identifier":"q43","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Visible physical access does not by itself establish that a door, path or work zone is the approved route; orient to the actual site plan and ask when route ownership or access is unclear.","content_classification":"crew_blueprint_framework","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Public accessibility, fire/egress and venue access decisions remain separate authority layers."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L91-DEPT-RELEASE","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-FLD","D-LTG","D-AUD","D-VID"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.1","block_identifier":"post-show-appearance","question_identifier":"q91","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The end of a performance or the appearance of idle gear does not by itself release a department's equipment or cable for strike; wait for the responsible department/lead to clear the work before moving it.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Release ownership varies by department/production; physical appearance is not acceptance evidence."}
{"content_id":"CL-SHF-FUND-L93-CALL-RELEASE","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.3","block_identifier":"strike-completion","question_identifier":"q93","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Finishing the main equipment move is not the same as being released from the call. Complete assigned cleanup/handoff, return borrowed items, check in through the controlling process and leave only after actual release/sign-out requirements are satisfied.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact release and sign-out/timekeeping procedures vary by employer/local/CBA/venue."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q14A","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.4","block_identifier":"scenario-call-time","question_identifier":"q14a","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Call time is 8:00 AM and the worker is still walking from parking at 7:57 without checking in. Correct answer: the worker should already be through the required check-in and ready to receive direction.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"work_readiness","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests readiness/check-in, not a universal minutes-early rule."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q14A","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.4","block_identifier":"scenario-call-time-coaching","question_identifier":"q14a","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Call time is treated as readiness/availability through the controlling check-in process in the recurring work rules used here; exact early-arrival expectations vary by call.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"low","authority_implication":"work_readiness","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L14-CHECKIN."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q14B","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.4","block_identifier":"scenario-task-completion","question_identifier":"q14b","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The worker finishes an assignment while other departments remain busy. Correct answer: report completion or return to the assigned lead for direction, rather than self-assigning or assuming a break.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests task completion/reassignment boundary."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q14B","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.4","block_identifier":"scenario-task-completion-coaching","question_identifier":"q14b","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Useful availability means returning through the established work-assignment process; task completion alone does not create cross-department authority, a break, or release.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L14-REPORTBACK."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q14C","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.4","block_identifier":"scenario-specialized-task","question_identifier":"q14c","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A tech asks the learner to perform an unfamiliar specialized task. Correct answer: state the limitation honestly and ask for instruction or another assignment rather than improvising.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests authority/competence boundary, not a technical procedure."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q14C","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"1","lesson_identifier":"1.4","block_identifier":"scenario-specialized-task-coaching","question_identifier":"q14c","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Honest limits preserve work control. Observation or course exposure does not create employer authorization or specialist competence for an unfamiliar task.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L14-LIMITS."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q43","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-FLD","D-LOG","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.3","block_identifier":"new-space-hazards","question_identifier":"q43","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"In a new venue with an unknown cable, an open door and forklift blind-spot exposure, correct behavior is to avoid assumptions and ask about all three before acting.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Assesses orientation/ownership/equipment-traffic judgment."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q43","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-FLD","D-LOG","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"4","lesson_identifier":"4.3","block_identifier":"new-space-hazards-coaching","question_identifier":"q43","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Orientation means identifying what is controlled or unknown before acting: do not move an un-released cable, infer route approval from appearance, or occupy equipment blind spots.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from cable-ownership, route-verification and PIT-pedestrian claims."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q62","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"5.2","block_identifier":"availability-decision","question_identifier":"q62","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The worker finishes an assignment while another department is busy. Correct answer: check back with the assigned lead or remain ready where directed rather than independently joining the other department or taking an assumed break.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests availability to controlling work structure."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q62","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"5.2","block_identifier":"availability-decision-coaching","question_identifier":"q62","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Availability to the established lead prevents uncoordinated cross-department self-assignment; task completion alone does not create release or a break.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L14-REPORTBACK."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q91","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-FLD","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.1","block_identifier":"post-show-appearance","question_identifier":"q91","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"The show ends and department gear/cable appears unused. Correct answer: wait for the responsible department/lead to explicitly clear it before moving it.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests explicit release rather than inference from appearance."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q91","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-FLD","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.1","block_identifier":"post-show-appearance-coaching","question_identifier":"q91","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Strike begins when the owning department/work process actually releases the system; the end of the show or apparent idleness is not sufficient evidence by itself.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from CL-SHF-FUND-L91-DEPT-RELEASE."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q93","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.3","block_identifier":"strike-completion","question_identifier":"q93","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Main equipment is loaded but cleanup remains and no formal release has occurred. Correct answer: continue assigned cleanup, keep exits clear, return borrowed items, check in and remain until formally released.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Tests call completion/release plus egress/reset discipline."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q93","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-CAR","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R1","authority_class":"A1","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.3","block_identifier":"strike-completion-coaching","question_identifier":"q93","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A complete call includes the assigned cleanup/handoff and the actual release/sign-out process; emergency exit routes remain clear while that work continues.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from release and egress claims."}
